#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""factory-dispatch — resolve the run_agents parameters for one factory child step.

This is the deterministic MECHANICS half of the foreman's job: given a chosen
track (triage / spec / implementation / code-review) and a prompt brief, it
resolves the target subagent's CONFIG (base skill + model) + the shared
environment and emits a ready-to-use `run_agents` tool-call payload as JSON. The
foreman then dispatches the child by CALLING the `run_agents` tool with that
payload — the actual child run is launched by the platform's orchestration tool,
not by this script. This script performs NO network I/O and hits NO API.

It contains NO routing JUDGMENT — deciding *which* track a request belongs to
is the foreman's job (the factory-foreman skill). This script only resolves a
track to its config and composes the `run_agents` arguments, mirroring the thin,
deterministic style of factory-state (resolve config, compose JSON, fail loud).

Dispatch is BY CONFIG, not by identity: each subagent's skill/model is applied
inline in the `run_agents` payload and the child executes as the foreman itself
(the `run_agents` tool links the child to the calling foreman run automatically).
There is no `agent_identity_uid` to set: the foreman runs as a service account,
and the server forbids a service-account caller from setting a different
execution principal ("agents cannot specify a different execution principal").
Reconstructing the config inline keeps execution principal = foreman while still
giving the child the right skills/model.

skill + model are per-track (from <track>/config.json);
environment_id is shared and comes from the agent's environment
(FACTORY_FOREMAN_ENV), like the Jira API token comes from $JIRA_API_TOKEN.

Resolution order for skill (per track), first wins:
  1. explicit flag (--skill)
  2. env var override (FACTORY_FOREMAN_<TRACK>_SKILL; TRACK upper,
     hyphens -> underscores, e.g. code-review -> CODE_REVIEW)
  3. derived from <track>/config.json:
     <repos.self>:<track>/.agents/skills/<agent.entrypoint_skill>/SKILL.md
The resolved skill is emitted as a `run_agents` skills[] entry (a
repository-qualified `org/repo:path/to/SKILL.md` spec) so the tool attaches it
to the child; the child brief also names it as the entry point to read first.

Resolution order for model (per track, optional), first wins:
  1. explicit flag (--model)
  2. env var override (FACTORY_FOREMAN_<TRACK>_MODEL)
  3. model in <track>/config.json (a plain model-id string, e.g. "auto").
The resolved model is emitted as `run_agents` `model_id`.

Every dispatched child run is NAMED deterministically as
FA_<track>_<current UTC timestamp> (e.g. FA_triage_2024-04-15T14:30 — the track
is a single token with no spaces and the timestamp is the current UTC time to
the minute) unless an explicit --name is passed, which wins (see
_build_run_name). The name is emitted as the child's `run_agents`
agent_run_configs[].name.

Resolution order for environment_id (shared), first wins:
  1. explicit flag (--environment)
  2. agent environment variable (FACTORY_FOREMAN_ENV)
If unresolved, the `run_agents` tool's own default environment applies (the child
inherits the foreman's environment); it is never hardcoded in config. When
resolved, it is emitted as `run_agents` remote.environment_id.

Resolution order for parent run id (names the foreman run the child reports step
  completion to; embedded in the coordination footer of the child brief), first
  wins:
  1. explicit flag (--parent-run-id) — PREFERRED; pass the foreman's current
     run id explicitly so the child always reports to the live foreman.
  2. CURRENT_RUN_ID env var (the runtime-provided / current foreman run id)
  3. OZ_RUN_ID env var (the dispatching foreman's run id, injected by the
     worker at launch). This is only set at launch, so it can be STALE after a
     resume / follow-up and name an older foreman run. To avoid the child
     reporting completion to the wrong (stale) foreman, prefer 1 or 2 over it,
     and a divergence between these signals is warned about loudly on stderr.
Note the `run_agents` tool also links the child to the calling foreman run
automatically; the footer's embedded id is what the child messages on step
completion, and downstream skills read it as `parent_run_id`.

Resolution order for the Oz web origin (used only to build the child's run link
after the tool returns its run id), first wins:
  1. explicit flag (--api-url) host, mapped to its Oz web host
  2. FACTORY_FOREMAN_API_URL env var host, mapped to its Oz web host
  3. https://oz.warp.dev (mapped from the production default)
The child run link is <oz-web-origin>/runs/<run_id>, the same "View run in Oz"
page the Slack / Jira integrations link to. This script does not know the run
id (the `run_agents` tool returns it as agent_id), so it emits `oz_web_origin`
and `run_link_template` and the foreman substitutes the returned id. The runs
API and the Oz web app are served from DIFFERENT hosts (e.g. API staging.warp.dev
vs web oz.staging.warp.dev; API app.warp.dev vs web oz.warp.dev), so the web
origin is mapped from the API host rather than reused verbatim — see
_oz_web_origin.

A still-unresolved (or placeholder REPLACE_ME) skill or parent run id fails
loudly with the flag/env-var to set. model and environment_id are optional; if
unresolved, the tool's own defaults apply.

The child brief is PREPENDED with the track's standing playbook
(<track>/AGENTS.md) so the child receives its full track role/playbook in
addition to the foreman's brief handoff description. A missing or empty AGENTS.md
is a non-fatal warning; the brief alone still dispatches. The playbook is emitted
as the shared `run_agents` base_prompt (prepended to every child prompt); the
task brief + coordination footer are emitted as the per-child prompt.

The child brief is suffixed with a deterministic COORDINATION FOOTER (built
from the resolved parent run id) so the foreman's step-gated state machine works
without each subagent skill hardcoding the foreman's id: it tells the child to
message the foreman on STEP COMPLETION (after it applies the next gate label),
to route any gating ask - on either door - through the foreman as a `RELAY:`
message (children cannot post to the task's conversation; only the foreman can
speak in the originating chat thread or in the Jira-door conversation the Warp
app mirrors, and a service-account Jira comment's replies are not routed to
the factory), and to simply end if agent-to-agent messaging is unavailable
(the foreman then advances off the ticket's gate label).

Computer use is ENABLED by default on every dispatched child
(remote.computer_use_enabled=true in the emitted payload). The `run_agents` tool
otherwise defaults it to false, which would leave children without the
computer_use tool and unable to satisfy the factory-verification mandate (triage
reproducing UI defects, implementation / review capturing and checking
screenshot proof for user-facing changes). Pass --no-computer-use to opt a
specific run out.

Python 3 stdlib only.
"""

import argparse
import json
import os
import sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from urllib.parse import urlparse

SCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(SCRIPT_DIR)
AGENTS_DIR = REPO_ROOT

TRACKS = ("triage", "spec", "implementation", "code-review")
PLACEHOLDER = "REPLACE_ME"

# The per-track standing playbook lives next to the track's config.json.
AGENTS_MD_FILENAME = "AGENTS.md"

# Prepended (with the track's AGENTS.md text) to the child brief so the child
# reads its standing track playbook before the foreman's specific task brief.
# Emitted as the shared run_agents base_prompt.
TRACK_AGENTS_MD_HEADER = (
    "# Track playbook - {track}/AGENTS.md\n"
    "This is the standing playbook for your track. Read it first, then act on "
    "the task brief that follows.\n\n"
)
# Fallback base_prompt when the track has no AGENTS.md playbook: still point the
# child at its attached entry skill so dispatch works without a playbook.
FALLBACK_BASE_PROMPT = (
    "You are the factory {track} child step dispatched by the foreman. Read and "
    "follow your attached entry skill, then act on the task brief that follows."
)

# Appended to every child brief (when a parent run id is resolved) so the
# foreman can drive the step-gated loop. Keep this in sync with the foreman's
# factory-foreman skill and the subagents' terminal-handoff steps.
COORDINATION_FOOTER = (
    "\n\n---\n"
    "**Foreman coordination.** You are running as a child step of the factory "
    "foreman (agent run id: {parent_run_id}). When your step is **complete** - "
    "after you have applied the next pipeline gate label and posted your "
    "artifacts to the ticket - send a brief completion message to the foreman "
    "at that run id (via your agent-to-agent messaging tool) summarizing the "
    "result, the artifacts you created (tracker issue / spec PR / PR / "
    "review links + your Oz run link), and the gate label you applied, "
    "then end your turn. If your step instead **pauses for required human "
    "input** (a clarifying question, spec approval, or any other gating ask): "
    "you CANNOT post to the task's conversation yourself on either door - "
    "only the foreman can speak in the originating chat thread (e.g. the "
    "Slack thread) or in the Jira-door conversation (the Warp app mirrors "
    "the foreman's responses onto the ticket), so never attempt to post "
    "there or hunt for a way in, and NEVER post a gating ask as a "
    "service-account Jira comment via `scripts/tracker comment` - replies "
    "to service-account comments are not routed to the factory, so never "
    "tell anyone to reply to one. Instead send the foreman a relay message "
    "(agent-to-agent, to the run id above) with the subject prefixed "
    "`RELAY:` and a body containing the exact, ready-to-post text of the "
    "ask (Slack mrkdwn on a Slack-door task, plain markdown on a Jira-door "
    "task; written for a stranger); the foreman posts it to the conversation "
    "verbatim and forwards the human's reply back to you as a message that "
    "resumes you. Either way, record the durable content on the ticket "
    "and end your turn. A `RELAY:` message is NOT a completion report - the "
    "step is still incomplete and the foreman keeps waiting; send the "
    "completion message only once the step actually completes. If "
    "agent-to-agent messaging is unavailable, record the ask durably on the "
    "ticket (on a Slack-door task a record comment noting the conversation "
    "channel was unreachable; on a Jira-door task a description append via "
    "`scripts/tracker update-issue --append-description` - never a "
    "service-account comment there), and end; on "
    "completion just end after applying the label - the foreman advances off "
    "the ticket's gate label."
)

# Only used to derive the Oz web origin for the child's run link (no API call is
# ever made). Kept as an API-shaped URL so the same host->Oz-web-host mapping and
# the FACTORY_FOREMAN_API_URL override that factory-eval uses keeps working.
DEFAULT_API_URL = "https://app.warp.dev/api/v1/agent/runs"


def _die(msg):
    print(f"factory-dispatch: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def _warn(msg):
    """Emit a non-fatal warning to stderr (does not affect stdout JSON)."""
    print(f"factory-dispatch: warning: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)


def _env_key(track):
    return track.upper().replace("-", "_")


def _load_json(path, what):
    """Read a JSON object from path, or None if absent. Fails loud on errors."""
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        return None
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            data = json.load(fh)
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:
        _die(f"could not read {what} {path}: {e}")
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        _die(f"{what} {path} must be a JSON object")
    return data


def _config_path(track):
    return os.path.join(AGENTS_DIR, track, "config.json")


def _load_config(track):
    """Load a track's config.json, failing loud if it is missing."""
    data = _load_json(_config_path(track), f"{track} config")
    if data is None:
        _die(f"no config for track {track!r}: expected {_config_path(track)}")
    return data


def _agents_md_path(track):
    return os.path.join(AGENTS_DIR, track, AGENTS_MD_FILENAME)


def _load_track_agents_md(track):
    """Load the track's AGENTS.md playbook text, or None if absent/empty.

    This is the standing per-track playbook that lives next to the track's
    config.json (<track>/AGENTS.md). It is prepended to every child brief
    so the child gets its full track role/playbook in addition to the foreman's
    brief handoff. A missing/empty file is a non-fatal warning: the brief alone
    still dispatches. A read error fails loud.
    """
    path = _agents_md_path(track)
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        _warn(f"no AGENTS.md for track {track!r}: expected {path}")
        return None
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            text = fh.read().strip()
    except OSError as e:
        _die(f"could not read {track} AGENTS.md {path}: {e}")
    if not text:
        _warn(f"{track} AGENTS.md {path} is empty")
        return None
    return text


def _build_base_prompt(track):
    """Build the shared run_agents base_prompt from the track's AGENTS.md.

    The base_prompt is prepended to every child prompt by the run_agents tool, so
    it carries the standing track playbook. When no AGENTS.md is available, fall
    back to a minimal lead-in that still points the child at its attached entry
    skill so dispatch works without a playbook.
    """
    agents_md = _load_track_agents_md(track)
    if not agents_md:
        return FALLBACK_BASE_PROMPT.format(track=track)
    return TRACK_AGENTS_MD_HEADER.format(track=track) + agents_md


def _derive_skill(track, config):
    """Derive the repo-qualified base SKILL.md spec for a track from its config.

    <repos.self>:<track>/.agents/skills/<agent.entrypoint_skill>/SKILL.md.
    Returns None if entrypoint_skill or repos.self is unset/placeholder.
    """
    agent = config.get("agent")
    entry = agent.get("entrypoint_skill") if isinstance(agent, dict) else None
    repos = config.get("repos")
    repo = repos.get("self") if isinstance(repos, dict) else None
    if not entry or entry == PLACEHOLDER:
        return None
    if not repo or repo == PLACEHOLDER:
        return None
    return f"{repo}:{track}/.agents/skills/{entry}/SKILL.md"


def _resolve_skill(track, flag, config):
    """Resolve the base skill via flag -> env var -> derived from config."""
    if flag and flag != PLACEHOLDER:
        return flag
    env_val = os.environ.get(f"FACTORY_FOREMAN_{_env_key(track)}_SKILL")
    if env_val and env_val != PLACEHOLDER:
        return env_val
    return _derive_skill(track, config)


def _resolve_model(track, flag, config):
    """Resolve the model via flag -> env var -> config (optional).

    The config `model` must be a plain model-id string (e.g. "auto"). Returns
    None when unresolved, in which case the run_agents tool's own default
    applies.
    """
    if flag and flag != PLACEHOLDER:
        return flag
    env_val = os.environ.get(f"FACTORY_FOREMAN_{_env_key(track)}_MODEL")
    if env_val and env_val != PLACEHOLDER:
        return env_val
    val = config.get("model")
    if isinstance(val, dict):
        _die(
            f"model for track {track!r} must be a plain model-id string, "
            f"not a JSON object"
        )
    if val and val != PLACEHOLDER:
        return val
    return None


# Prefix for every auto-generated factory run name: FA_<track>_<timestamp>.
RUN_NAME_PREFIX = "FA"


def _build_run_name(explicit_name, track):
    """Build the dispatched child run's name.

    An explicit --name wins; otherwise the run is named deterministically as
    FA_<track>_<current UTC timestamp> (e.g. FA_triage_2024-04-15T14:30). The
    track is a single token with no spaces (triage / spec / implementation /
    code-review) and the timestamp is the current UTC time to the minute
    (%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M).
    """
    if explicit_name:
        return explicit_name
    timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M")
    return f"{RUN_NAME_PREFIX}_{track}_{timestamp}"


def _resolve_environment(flag):
    """Resolve the shared environment id (applies to every track).

    Order: --environment flag -> FACTORY_FOREMAN_ENV (the agent environment
    variable, like $JIRA_API_TOKEN). PLACEHOLDER is treated as unset; returns
    None when unresolved, in which case the run_agents tool's default
    environment applies (the child inherits the foreman's environment). The
    environment id is never hardcoded in config.
    """
    if flag and flag != PLACEHOLDER:
        return flag
    env_val = os.environ.get("FACTORY_FOREMAN_ENV")
    if env_val and env_val != PLACEHOLDER:
        return env_val
    return None


def _clean_run_id(value):
    """Normalize a run-id candidate: empty / PLACEHOLDER -> None."""
    if value and value != PLACEHOLDER:
        return value
    return None


def _resolve_parent_run_id(flag):
    """Resolve the parent run id that the child reports step completion to.

    The child reports step completion to this run id, so it MUST name the live
    foreman. Order (first wins):
      1. --parent-run-id flag (PREFERRED — explicit current foreman run id)
      2. CURRENT_RUN_ID env (the runtime-provided / current foreman run id)
      3. OZ_RUN_ID env (worker-injected at launch; may be STALE after a resume
         / follow-up and name an older foreman run)

    A real dispatch fails before emitting a payload if this is unresolved. When
    these signals disagree, warn loudly: a stale $OZ_RUN_ID (or a wrong explicit
    value) would make the child report completion to the wrong foreman.
    """
    flag_val = _clean_run_id(flag)
    current_val = _clean_run_id(os.environ.get("CURRENT_RUN_ID"))
    oz_val = _clean_run_id(os.environ.get("OZ_RUN_ID"))

    if flag_val is not None:
        resolved, source = flag_val, "--parent-run-id"
    elif current_val is not None:
        resolved, source = current_val, "$CURRENT_RUN_ID"
    elif oz_val is not None:
        resolved, source = oz_val, "$OZ_RUN_ID"
    else:
        return None

    _warn_parent_run_id_divergence(resolved, source, flag_val, current_val, oz_val)
    return resolved


def _warn_parent_run_id_divergence(resolved, source, flag_val, current_val, oz_val):
    """Warn when the parent-run-id signals disagree.

    Guards the failure where the child reports to a stale foreman: $OZ_RUN_ID is
    set only at launch, so after a resume / follow-up it can name an older run.
    We compare it (and any explicit flag) against the runtime current id and warn
    on any divergence, naming which id is actually being used.
    """
    distinct = {v for v in (flag_val, current_val, oz_val) if v is not None}
    if len(distinct) <= 1:
        return
    # The classic stale case: $OZ_RUN_ID disagrees with the runtime current id.
    if current_val is not None and oz_val is not None and oz_val != current_val:
        _warn(
            f"$OZ_RUN_ID ({oz_val}) differs from the runtime current run id "
            f"$CURRENT_RUN_ID ({current_val}) and looks stale."
        )
    # An explicit value that disagrees with the runtime current id.
    if flag_val is not None and current_val is not None and flag_val != current_val:
        _warn(
            f"--parent-run-id ({flag_val}) differs from the runtime current run "
            f"id $CURRENT_RUN_ID ({current_val})."
        )
    _warn(
        f"using {resolved} (from {source}) as the parent run id; the child will "
        f"report step completion to that run. If it is not the current foreman, "
        f"pass --parent-run-id explicitly with the foreman's current run id."
    )


def _build_child_prompt(prompt, parent_run_id):
    """Build the per-child run_agents prompt (task brief + coordination footer).

    The coordination footer is only added when a parent run id is resolved so the
    child knows which run to report completion to. Without a parent run id the
    footer would name no foreman, so it is omitted. The track playbook is NOT
    included here — it is emitted separately as the shared base_prompt.
    """
    if not parent_run_id:
        return prompt
    return prompt + COORDINATION_FOOTER.format(parent_run_id=parent_run_id)


def _resolve_api_url(flag):
    """Resolve and validate the API-shaped URL used to derive the Oz web origin.

    No request is ever made to it; it is only mapped to the Oz web host that
    serves the child's /runs/<id> page (see _oz_web_origin). Order: --api-url ->
    FACTORY_FOREMAN_API_URL -> the production default.
    """
    value = flag or os.environ.get("FACTORY_FOREMAN_API_URL") or DEFAULT_API_URL
    value = value.rstrip("/")
    parsed = urlparse(value)
    if parsed.scheme not in ("http", "https") or not parsed.netloc:
        _die(f"invalid API URL {value!r}; expected an http(s) URL")
    return value


def _build_run_agents_payload(
    skill,
    base_prompt,
    child_prompt,
    model,
    environment_id,
    name,
    track,
    computer_use_enabled,
):
    """Compose the run_agents tool-call arguments for one factory child step.

    The foreman calls the run_agents tool with this payload verbatim (a single
    agent_run_configs entry for a single-child dispatch). Run-wide fields
    (skills, model_id, remote) are shared; the per-child prompt carries the task
    brief + coordination footer.
    """
    remote = {"computer_use_enabled": computer_use_enabled}
    if environment_id:
        remote["environment_id"] = environment_id
    agent_run_config = {
        "name": name or f"factory-{track}",
        "title": f"factory {track}",
        "prompt": child_prompt,
    }
    payload = {
        "summary": (
            f"Dispatch the factory {track} child step for the current request."
        ),
        "base_prompt": base_prompt,
        "skills": [{"spec": skill}],
        "remote": remote,
        "agent_run_configs": [agent_run_config],
    }
    if model:
        payload["model_id"] = model
    return payload


# The public runs API and the Oz web app are served from DIFFERENT hosts: the
# API lives on e.g. staging.warp.dev / app.warp.dev, while the run page the Slack
# / Jira integrations link to (and humans open) lives on the Oz web host —
# oz.staging.warp.dev / oz.warp.dev. Deriving the web link straight from the API
# origin yields a 404, so map known API hosts to their Oz web host.
OZ_WEB_HOST_BY_API_HOST = {
    "staging.warp.dev": "oz.staging.warp.dev",
    "app.warp.dev": "oz.warp.dev",
}


def _oz_web_origin(api_url):
    """Map the API URL's origin to the Oz web origin that serves /runs/<id>.

    The runs API and the Oz web app live on different hosts (see
    OZ_WEB_HOST_BY_API_HOST). For a known API host we return its mapped Oz web
    host; for anything else (custom deploy / localhost) we fall back to the API
    origin unchanged so local development keeps working.
    """
    parsed = urlparse(api_url)
    web_host = OZ_WEB_HOST_BY_API_HOST.get(parsed.netloc, parsed.netloc)
    return f"{parsed.scheme}://{web_host}"


def main():
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="factory-dispatch",
        description=(
            "Resolve the run_agents tool-call parameters for one factory child "
            "step, applying the track's config (skill + model). "
            "Resolves config per track from <track>/config.json + the "
            "shared environment from the agent environment variable "
            "$FACTORY_FOREMAN_ENV (flag -> env var), names the run "
            "FA_<track>_<UTC timestamp>, and emits "
            "{track,skill,model,name,environment_id,"
            "computer_use_enabled,parent_run_id,"
            "oz_web_origin,run_link_template,run_agents} as JSON. The foreman "
            "then CALLS the run_agents tool with the emitted `run_agents` "
            "payload; this script makes NO API call. Mechanics only: the "
            "foreman decides the track."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--api-url",
        help=(
            "API-shaped URL used ONLY to derive the Oz web origin for the "
            "child's run link (no request is made). Defaults to "
            "$FACTORY_FOREMAN_API_URL, then the production endpoint."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--track",
        required=True,
        choices=TRACKS,
        help="Which subagent to route to.",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--prompt",
        required=True,
        help=(
            "The task brief handed to the child run (verbatim request + "
            "context). The track's <track>/AGENTS.md playbook is emitted "
            "as the shared base_prompt and the coordination footer is appended "
            "to the per-child prompt."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--name",
        help=(
            "Optional human-readable name for the child run. When omitted, the "
            "run is named FA_<track>_<UTC timestamp> "
            "(e.g. FA_triage_2024-04-15T14:30)."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--skill",
        help="Override the resolved base skill for this track.",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--model",
        help="Override the resolved base model for this track.",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--environment",
        help="Override the resolved (shared) environment id for this run.",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--parent-run-id",
        help=(
            "The foreman run id the child reports step completion to (embedded "
            "in the coordination footer). PREFERRED: pass the foreman's current "
            "run id explicitly. Falls back to $CURRENT_RUN_ID, then $OZ_RUN_ID "
            "(which is set only at launch and may be stale). Required for a real "
            "dispatch."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--computer-use",
        dest="computer_use",
        action="store_true",
        default=True,
        help=(
            "Enable the computer_use tool for the child run (DEFAULT). Factory "
            "children need it to reproduce/validate user-facing changes and "
            "capture screenshot proof per factory-verification; the run_agents "
            "tool otherwise defaults computer use off."
        ),
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--no-computer-use",
        dest="computer_use",
        action="store_false",
        help=(
            "Disable the computer_use tool for the child run. Use only for a run "
            "that genuinely cannot have a user-facing effect to validate."
        ),
    )
    args = parser.parse_args()

    config = _load_config(args.track)
    skill = _resolve_skill(args.track, args.skill, config)
    if not skill:
        key = _env_key(args.track)
        _die(
            f"no base skill for track {args.track!r}: set --skill, "
            f"$FACTORY_FOREMAN_{key}_SKILL, or agent.entrypoint_skill + "
            f"repos.self in {_config_path(args.track)}"
        )
    model = _resolve_model(args.track, args.model, config)
    run_name = _build_run_name(args.name, args.track)
    environment_id = _resolve_environment(args.environment)
    parent_run_id = _resolve_parent_run_id(args.parent_run_id)
    if not parent_run_id:
        _die(
            "no parent run id: pass --parent-run-id (preferred) with the "
            "foreman's current run id, or ensure $CURRENT_RUN_ID / $OZ_RUN_ID "
            "contains the dispatching foreman's run id"
        )
    api_url = _resolve_api_url(args.api_url)
    oz_web_origin = _oz_web_origin(api_url)
    base_prompt = _build_base_prompt(args.track)
    child_prompt = _build_child_prompt(args.prompt, parent_run_id)
    run_agents = _build_run_agents_payload(
        skill,
        base_prompt,
        child_prompt,
        model,
        environment_id,
        run_name,
        args.track,
        args.computer_use,
    )

    result = {
        "track": args.track,
        "skill": skill,
        "model": model,
        "name": run_name,
        "environment_id": environment_id,
        "computer_use_enabled": args.computer_use,
        "parent_run_id": parent_run_id,
        "oz_web_origin": oz_web_origin,
        "run_link_template": f"{oz_web_origin}/runs/{{run_id}}",
        "run_agents": run_agents,
    }
    json.dump(result, sys.stdout, indent=2)
    sys.stdout.write("\n")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
